  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) with a very low validation accuracy of 48.5%, leaving almost no evidence about which modality or representation carries signal for this task. The most fundamental uncertainty is whether image features alone are informative. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) tests this directly with the simplest image configuration, providing a clean cross-modality comparison to config_001. If image accuracy is substantially higher, it identifies image as the key signal and justifies investing subsequent experiments in multimodal fusion; if it is similarly low, it indicates the task is intrinsically difficult and we should prioritize better RNA representations or multiprofile aggregation; if it is lower, RNA is the stronger modality. This single experiment resolves the most consequential unknown for the entire search and is the highest-information next step under a limited budget."
}

